{
  "_comment": [
    "Bucket spec for /stats/home treatmentSubcategories.",
    "",
    "Each bucket can match terms three ways (apply in order; OR-combined within a bucket):",
    "  parentSubtreeUris — ontology parent URIs; expanded via OntologyService.getChildren",
    "                      (CHEBI must be loaded for these to populate; otherwise 0).",
    "  uriPrefixes       — exact valueUri prefix match (startsWith).",
    "  uriExactMatches   — full-URI equality match.",
    "",
    "Bucket order is first-match-wins: a term that's both a drug AND a hormone lands",
    "in the bucket listed first.",
    "",
    "Two catchalls are emitted automatically:",
    "  other_chemical   — CHEBI URIs not in any explicit bucket.",
    "  other            — non-CHEBI URIs not in any explicit bucket.",
    "",
    "To override: drop a treatment-buckets.json into ${gemma.appdata.home}/HomeStats/.",
    "If present it replaces this classpath default. Otherwise this file ships."
  ],
  "buckets": [
    {
      "_comment": "Vehicles / solvent controls. Listed FIRST so e.g. DMSO matches `vehicle` before falling through into the broader CHEBI:23888 'drug' subtree under `approved_drug`. The UI can hide this bucket from the bar chart — it's not pharmacology data, but worth classifying so curators can see what's there.",
      "key": "vehicle",
      "label": "Vehicles / solvents",
      "uriExactMatches": [
        "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_28262",
        "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_16236",
        "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_15377",
        "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_32588",
        "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_26710",
        "http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0002677",
        "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0100046"
      ]
    },
    {
      "_comment": "Subtree URIs ARE preferred — they auto-pick-up new CHEBI terms — but they require CHEBI loaded in OntologyService. As a fallback, each bucket also carries a curated uriExactMatches list of CHEBI IDs we know belong in it. When CHEBI is loaded, the subtree expansion catches everything in it; when not, the exact list still gives a useful bucket. Either way: this list can be edited without recompile.",
      "key": "approved_drug",
      "label": "Approved drugs",
      "parentSubtreeUris": ["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_23888"],
      "uriExactMatches": [
        "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_50845",
        "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_41879",
